AIM - To implement Single Area OSPF (Open Shortest Path First) routing protocol using Cisco Packet Tracer.
1. TOPOLOGY
Add these devices:
- 4 Routers (1841)
- 1 Switch (2960)
Connections:
1. R0 → Switch
2. R1 → Switch
3. R2 → Switch
4. R2 → R3 (Serial connection)

3. CONFIGURE ROUTER R0
enable
configure terminal
interface loopback 0
ip address 10.10.20.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 192.168.0.2 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
end
write memory

4. CONFIGURE ROUTER R1
enable
configure terminal
interface loopback 0
ip address 10.10.10.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 192.168.0.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
end
write memory

5. CONFIGURE ROUTER R2
enable
configure terminal
interface loopback 0
ip address 10.10.30.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
interface serial 0/1/0
ip address 172.16.0.1 255.255.255.252
no shutdown
exit
interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 192.168.0.3 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
end
write memory


6. CONFIGURE ROUTER R3
enable
configure terminal
interface loopback 0
ip address 10.10.40.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
interface serial 0/1/0
ip address 172.16.0.2 255.255.255.252
no shutdown
exit
end
write memory


7. CONFIGURE OSPF PROTOCOL
Now we configure OSPF on all four routers.
Configure OSPF on R0
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 1
router-id 10.2.2.2
network 10.10.20.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
network 192.168.0.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
end
write memory

Configure OSPF on R1
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 1
router-id 10.1.1.1
network 10.10.10.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
network 192.168.0.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
end
write memory


Configure OSPF on R2
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 1
router-id 10.3.3.3
network 10.10.30.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
network 172.16.0.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
network 192.168.0.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
end
write memory


Configure OSPF on R3
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 1
router-id 10.4.4.4
network 10.10.40.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
network 172.16.0.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
end
write memory

8. CHECK CONNECTIVITY
Run these commands on the routers.
Check routing table:
show ip route
Check OSPF neighbors:
show ip ospf neighbor
Check connectivity from R0:
ping 10.10.10.1
ping 10.10.30.1
ping 10.10.40.1
Check connectivity from R3:
ping 10.10.30.1
ping 10.10.20.1
ping 10.10.10.1
